17592186439429} {:answer/id #uuid "6bc375ff-fae1-5c3f-a326-bc262ba269ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439430}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2c538ce5-ccb5-5dd4-83dc-819839f73fd1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439429} :answer-field/id #uuid "2fdeb008-c261-5a02-bdfb-70133c5efaf5" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440072}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "163eeae3-71ad-5b66-a0aa-4b05d346c12b" :question/math-academy-id "q-113525" :question/problem "Calculate the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{3}{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+7x}.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $x=-7$\n- **II.** $x=-1$\n- **III.** $x=0$\n- **IV.** $x=1$" :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{3}{{x}^{3}+{x}^{2}+7x} \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{x({x}^{2}+x+7)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThere are no common factors in the numerator and denominator, so we set the denominator equal to zero. This gives\n\n$$\nx({x}^{2}+x+7)=0.\n$$\n\nWe now solve the above equation using the zero product property:\n\n- Solving $x=0$ gives the solution $x=0.$\n\n- The equation ${x}^{2}+x+7=0$ has no real solutions because the discriminant $D$ is negative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={b}^{2}-4ac \\\\  & ={1}^{2}-4(1)(7) \\\\  & =1-28 \\\\  & =-27.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the only vertical asymptote is $x=0.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247371 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087845 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4b0b57da-f9af-5fab-a337-51ee4cb28f9e" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating Vertical Asymptotes With Common Factors When the Denominator Has Complex Roots"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fb9d7b25-5854-520d-8ebf-a6801866a103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439439} {:answer/id #uuid "7bd9b49f-1e1e-558e-9235-e08d3e02c10b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439440}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fb9d7b25-5854-520d-8ebf-a6801866a103" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439439} :answer-field/id #uuid "a9087893-bc60-52fc-8d81-3cedf3411ac6" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440077} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "07ddf72a-287c-5883-9635-ec2b9399d667" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439441} {:answer/id #uuid "59344e22-da7e-5c4e-9b1f-2a9bd6abb444" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439442}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "07ddf72a-287c-5883-9635-ec2b9399d667" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439441} :answer-field/id #uuid "a46f02c4-4697-588e-bc3e-a16a5e0bec49" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440078} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "044decdf-112a-5933-b2b2-02be3db90f11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439443} {:answer/id #uuid "91341243-61ec-5cbb-8cb0-aa4b45e28585" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439444}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "044decdf-112a-5933-b2b2-02be3db90f11" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439443} :answer-field/id #uuid "f27daf57-7ce5-534a-ba37-ad6313ed2cc9" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440079}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "daec1f65-9c08-5df4-939b-bebb2395a749" :question/math-academy-id "q-113545" :question/problem "Calculate the vertical asymptotes of $f(x)=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}}.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $x=-1$\n- **II.** $x=0$\n- **III.** $x=1$" :question/worked-solution "To find the vertical asymptotes of a rational function, we factor the numerator and denominator and cancel any common factors. Then, we set the denominator equal to zero and solve for $x.$\n\nFactoring the numerator and denominator and canceling any common factors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{4}+{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{x}^{2}({x}^{2}+x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\cancel{{x}^{2}}}{\\cancel{{x}^{2}}({x}^{2}+x+2)} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+x+2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we set the denominator equal to zero:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+x+2=0\n$$\n\nThis equation does not have any real solutions because the discriminant $D$ is negative:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}D & ={b}^{2}-4ac \\\\  & =1-4(1)(2) \\\\  & =-7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)$ has no vertical asymptotes."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262919 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124445 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e8d807a6-7896-5045-a14a-908b58831340" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points Where a Gradient Vanishes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8fe7a32f-bd64-5c3a-ac51-aa8e847ab23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439495} {:answer/id #uuid "a5b19982-26ea-52cf-bfb6-891798ebe687" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439496}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8fe7a32f-bd64-5c3a-ac51-aa8e847ab23c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439495} :answer-field/id #uuid "5c9b26fe-a648-553a-a416-e7a5675ab1fe" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440105} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8879c732-ca2d-5143-a4fe-4257993d10ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439497} {:answer/id #uuid "a9d1f38f-73c6-5480-a2d4-f3c457b36e82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439498}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a9d1f38f-73c6-5480-a2d4-f3c457b36e82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439498} :answer-field/id #uuid "71ac6491-2fe7-5147-88bb-c17f0c42377d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440106} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e9a47546-8467-57ce-8aa2-a8af7a03a45d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439499} {:answer/id #uuid "9a881647-dacf-5b22-a11c-6dbd54eab45c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439500}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9a881647-dacf-5b22-a11c-6dbd54eab45c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439500} :answer-field/id #uuid "c5b81800-b1bd-502a-8929-18d2b7af4a18" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440107} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c3587a5-2b35-5b4d-8516-1a3e694d12a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439501} {:answer/id #uuid "f8a10786-54a3-53dd-acf2-86b3f03692c0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439502}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c3587a5-2b35-5b4d-8516-1a3e694d12a8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439501} :answer-field/id #uuid "0962b3c3-8729-55fc-a737-e4fe61f7b385" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440108}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "48261b12-c86c-55b1-9e2a-f38acbfa450a" :question/math-academy-id "q-128517" :question/problem "Given that $f(x,y)={x}^{2}-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y,$ find the points $(x,y),$ for $0\\le y<\\pi ,$ where $∇f(x,y)=0.$\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $(-1,0)$\n- **II.** $(0,\\frac{\\pi}{2})$\n- **III.** $(1,0)$\n- **IV.** $(1,\\frac{\\pi}{2})$" :question/worked-solution "First, we find the partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂f}{∂x} & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{2}-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & =2x-2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y \\\\ \\frac{∂f}{∂y} & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}({x}^{2}-2x\\operatorname{cos}⁡y) \\\\  & =2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, $∇f(x,y)=2(x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,i+2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j.$\n\nNow, we solve $∇f(x,y)=0:$ \n\n$$\n2(x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)\\,i+2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y\\,j=0\\text{ }i+0\\text{ }j\n$$\n\nSo, by equating the coefficients of $i$ and $j,$ we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{cases}2(x-\\operatorname{cos}⁡y)=0 \\\\ 2x\\operatorname{sin}⁡y=0\\end{cases}\n$$\n\nFrom the first equation, we get $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡y.$ Substituting this into the second equation, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{cos}⁡y\\operatorname{sin}⁡y & =0 \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}⁡2y & =0 \\\\ y & =0,\\,\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y=0,$ we get $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡0=1.$\n\n- For $y=\\frac{\\pi }{2},$ we get $x=\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\frac{\\pi }{2})=0.$\n\nTherefore, $∇f(x,y)=0,$ for $0\\le y<\\pi ,$ at two points: $(1,0)$ and $(0,\\frac{\\pi }{2}).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186265935 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186059849 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "ab642ad6-d9e0-5734-83b4-81627b9132eb" :knowledge-point/title "Solving for an Unknown Given the Determinant"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a96a6f2b-900e-5634-9638-19c6ba6bffea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439527} {:answer/id #uuid "5d1afda0-1dac-5620-821a-ad4de506b094" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439528}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a96a6f2b-900e-5634-9638-19c6ba6bffea" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439527} :answer-field/id #uuid "0a971e33-0a2